    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a 79.09 efficiency score, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an optimal intersection of a favorable matchup against Pallante and the high-value stolen base environment created by the pitcher's slow delivery. We are also projecting a strong showing from **Caleb Durbin** (65.78), whose score is buoyed by a favorable park factor and a soft matchup against Barnett. While we are currently awaiting official confirmation on **Caleb Durbin** and **Carson Benge**'s spots in the lineup, their projections remain high enough to justify immediate insertion into the active roster.\n\n**Lars Nootbaar** (59.86) edges out a crowded bench to earn the UTIL spot, largely due to a positive platoon advantage against Assad. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (55.92) remains a start despite facing a tougher arm in Winn, as his role in the three-hole provides enough volume to mitigate the SP skill penalty. **Chase Meidroth** (44.94) and **Carson Benge** (48.05) represent our marginal plays today; **Carson Benge** specifically carries a 35% rain risk, which warrants close monitoring as game time approaches. While we have roster depth including **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, none of these alternatives currently offer a more compelling efficiency profile than our active starters. With heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich** all idle today, we must maximize the efficiency of this current group to maintain our standing in the stolen base category.",
